WEBVTT

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:04.090
Over here.

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:08.150
That's amazing. So much has washed ashore.

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:09.000
Yes.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.900
I thought we could use this bamboo
to make a real roof for our shelter.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.800
Huh? Uh...

00:00:15.250 --> 00:00:17.430
We're gonna carry all of these back?

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:18.620
Don't worry.

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:20.610
There's a convenient way to do it.

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:25.440
We'll tie the bamboo together
like this to make rafts.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:27.080
Then we'll float them back along the coast.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:28.390
Oh, I see!

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:31.210
We'll use the rope to pull them to the shelter.

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:32.310
Yes.

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:35.320
But someone will have to ride and steer them.

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:36.550
What do you mean?

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:39.470
In short...

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:41.440
One person will ride each raft

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:44.600
and use a stick to keep it from
washing back onshore...

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:46.940
Like this. Simple, isn't it?

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:49.300
This drawing is... kinda scary.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.080
Is that a dead body?
Is it being dragged somewhere?

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:54.030
It's an explanation of the rafts!

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:03.740
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:06.540
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:57.260
Woohoo!

00:01:57.260 --> 00:01:59.520
It isn't too heavy, Homare-san?

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:00.800
I'm fine.

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:04.560
It's a technique that uses buoyancy
to transport heavy objects after all.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:07.590
Besides, with the motion of the waves,

00:02:07.590 --> 00:02:09.770
I'd think they'd be having
more problems than me.

00:02:09.770 --> 00:02:11.860
Hey, Shion. Make sure you—

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:20.740
We managed to get them here.
Now what should we do?

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.870
They're all different lengths, so...

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:25.620
let's cut them to sizes that are easier to use.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:29.850
I see. We'll use fire for that.

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:32.420
It's faster than a blade and more efficient.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:35.100
Right. Will you bring me the next piece?

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:36.170
Okay!

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:40.260
These are... pretty heavy...

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:43.630
Also... they might burst, so be careful.

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:45.140
Okay.

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:47.570
Are you all right?

00:02:47.570 --> 00:02:49.600
Yes... somehow...

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:53.520
If you're feeling better, then help us!

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:56.530
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:02:54.410 --> 00:02:56.530
I see...

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:00.640
We did it!

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:02.090
The roof is complete!

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:03.240
It's amazing!

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:05.180
Shade!

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:08.040
I thought it might feel a little
oppressive, but it seems fine.

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:12.950
Oh! When it rains it will run
down the roof into this gutter.

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:13.990
Awesome!

00:03:13.990 --> 00:03:15.960
We can use all the water
we want on rainy days!

00:03:15.960 --> 00:03:19.420
Now we can use the leftover
bamboo to make temporary tools.

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:20.130
Okay.

00:03:22.360 --> 00:03:25.350
Hey, Shion! Come help!

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:30.560
Picking up a spear to fight
is all too much for me.

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:34.050
More importantly, there wouldn't
happen to be any sweets lying around?

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:35.900
Will you hurry up and help?

00:03:40.190 --> 00:03:41.260
Huh? What's wrong?

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:42.700
Are you all right?

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:45.120
A bee?

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:47.140
It was scary!

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:49.890
I almost got stung!

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:52.850
I feel like we're seeing
bees more often lately...

00:03:52.850 --> 00:03:55.820
They might have built a hive nearby.

00:03:55.820 --> 00:03:57.080
Should we go look for it?

00:03:57.080 --> 00:03:57.880
No!

00:03:58.220 --> 00:04:00.550
It might be worth going.

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:07.550
Probably around here...

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:14.900
I can hear the buzzing
inside this fallen tree.

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:19.050
I see. The wind from
the shore doesn't reach here.

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:20.790
It's the perfect site for a hive.

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:22.850
This is no time to be impressed!

00:04:22.850 --> 00:04:25.410
It's not far from our shelter.
What are we gonna do?

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:26.890
Should we clear it out with fire?

00:04:26.890 --> 00:04:27.450
Huh?

00:04:27.450 --> 00:04:30.770
No. Burning the hive would be a waste.

00:04:31.240 --> 00:04:33.410
All right, Shion. It's time for sweets.

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:34.040
Huh?

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:35.810
Let's collect the honey.

00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:38.720
Listen well, Homare.

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:42.050
It is not uncommon for people
to die from bee stings.

00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:47.440
Any species of large bee or wasp
can cause shock symptoms with its sting.

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:46.390
Paper Wasp

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:47.720
Paper Wasp
Japanese Giant Hornet

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:51.060
The thing to be most worried about is an
allergic reaction to the poison in the stinger.

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:48.300
Japanese Giant Hornet

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:49.930
Japanese Giant Hornet
Carpenter Bee

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:50.350
Carpenter Bee

00:04:50.350 --> 00:04:51.060
Carpenter Bee
Honey Bee

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:54.810
There is a limit to the treatment
you can apply in a survival situation.

00:04:55.290 --> 00:04:56.760
You have to be very careful.

00:04:56.760 --> 00:04:57.660
Okay!

00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:02.540
An allergic reaction is possible
even with honey bees.

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:04.780
Please try not to get stung.

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:07.210
D-Don't get stung?

00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:08.720
We don't have anything to protect ourselves!

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:11.790
But we can't just leave it there either!

00:05:12.310 --> 00:05:15.190
We aren't getting nearly
enough carbohydrates.

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:20.250
Honey is roughly 80% sugar.
We can't afford to pass up the opportunity.

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:22.740
These days, everyone
is trying to cut back on carbs!

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:24.590
<i>Wasn't she just saying she wanted sweets?</i>

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:28.860
I will explain our plan of attack.

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:31.950
We'll place a torch in the hollow of the log,

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:33.970
and chase the bees out with smoke.

00:05:34.450 --> 00:05:37.970
We'll go into the log and collect
the comb with a knife.

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:42.250
Honeycomb is heavy, so we'll use
a relay sequence to carry it back.

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:44.150
Once we've collected the comb, we'll pull out.

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:47.820
At these temperatures,
the comb will be weaker.

00:05:48.190 --> 00:05:52.130
We must retrieve the comb before
the heat of the torch melts it.

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:53.990
It's a race against time!

00:05:56.760 --> 00:05:59.710
I've added things to this torch:
 prickly ash, which has a paralytic effect,

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:03.480
and Japanese mugwort, which repels bugs,
to increase the effects of the smoke.

00:06:10.630 --> 00:06:11.640
There're tons of them coming out!

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:14.430
Get down and stay still.

00:06:14.830 --> 00:06:16.270
Don't provoke them.

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:20.550
Even gentle honey bees
sting when they're upset.

00:06:20.890 --> 00:06:23.730
It's important to read the bees' mood.

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:27.190
They seem very upset right now.

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.150
<i>Well, they would be!</i>

00:06:35.140 --> 00:06:36.350
Almost...

00:06:37.070 --> 00:06:38.790
Okay! Let's go! Everyone!

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:40.670
There're still lots of bees!

00:06:40.670 --> 00:06:42.250
Homare-san!

00:06:47.310 --> 00:06:49.300
I've got one. Someone come get it.

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:52.000
No way! I can't! There're bees everywhere!

00:06:53.570 --> 00:06:54.970
She's been stung.

00:06:57.930 --> 00:06:58.770
Shion-san!

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:00.640
G-Got it.

00:07:01.840 --> 00:07:05.340
A-All right. Keep passing them to me.

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:16.450
Yes! We got the honey!

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:18.830
Now, now. Be gentle with it.

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:19.850
It's really honey!

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:21.500
Let's go ahead and extract it.

00:07:19.850 --> 00:07:21.500
It is!

00:07:22.730 --> 00:07:28.010
We'll cut the caps off the comb and use
the roof and gutter to collect the honey.

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:31.960
If we tried to squeeze it out,
we'd get too many impurities.

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:34.410
Oh! It's starting to pour out!

00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:38.850
Homare-san, is your hand all right?

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:41.590
Oh. I got stung a little, but...

00:07:41.590 --> 00:07:44.370
honey is supposed to be good for bee stings.

00:07:44.370 --> 00:07:45.590
Honey, right?

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:50.700
Are you all right? It doesn't hurt?

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:51.920
I'm fine.

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:54.910
My body doesn't have much
of a reaction to bee stings.

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:57.520
Um... Homare-san...

00:07:57.520 --> 00:07:59.240
I'm sorry for being selfish earli—

00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:01.790
It's so sweet!

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:04.390
It's the most wonderful of sweets, Homare-san!

00:08:04.390 --> 00:08:05.080
Right?

00:08:05.430 --> 00:08:07.480
Thank you so much.

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:09.890
We have so much!

00:08:09.890 --> 00:08:11.280
Yes!

00:08:09.890 --> 00:08:12.420
<i>I'm going to get stronger, too.</i>

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:15.430
<b>Are You Lost?</b>

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:15.430
<b>Replenishing Carbs...</b>

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:14.930
Really?

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:27.250
Wow! What is that?

00:08:27.250 --> 00:08:28.440
It's sole.

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:31.870
They hide in the sand.
You should look for them, too, Asuka.

00:08:31.870 --> 00:08:34.240
Use a bottle as a substitute for goggles.

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:42.360
I... I got one!

00:08:43.980 --> 00:08:46.170
Hey! Look at this!

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:47.790
Welcome back!

00:08:47.790 --> 00:08:49.010
What did you get?

00:08:49.010 --> 00:08:50.700
It's sole!

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:52.090
<i>I will, too.</i>

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:53.690
How's that? Awesome, right?

00:08:53.690 --> 00:08:55.040
Say, Homare-san...

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:57.510
Next time, I'd like to go fishing, too.

00:08:57.510 --> 00:09:00.090
Huh? Shion, you want to go fishing?

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:02.080
It's pretty tough, you know?

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:04.470
I can catch them, too!

00:09:04.470 --> 00:09:06.520
I'll catch something even
more amazing than that!

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:10.200
I wonder if there are any fish out there
dumb enough to get caught by you, Shion.

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:08.400
<i>Bats?</i>

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:11.800
<i>Where are those bats going?</i>

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:13.370
Of course there are!

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:16.150
Homare-san! Are you listening?

00:09:16.150 --> 00:09:19.350
Oh, right. Then I'll be 
counting on you tomorrow.

00:09:23.050 --> 00:09:25.040
I'm going to catch a big one!

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:26.540
You seem excited.

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:31.400
Well, we're off to check
the traps and collect firewood!

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:33.170
Good luck, Shion!

00:09:33.540 --> 00:09:35.120
Leave it to me!

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:39.550
Since you can't dive, let's use this raft.

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:40.790
All right.

00:09:41.950 --> 00:09:43.690
It rocks quite a bit...

00:09:43.690 --> 00:09:44.850
Be careful!

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:47.070
All right. Time to catch something!

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:51.420
Oh! There're lots down there!

00:09:51.420 --> 00:09:52.990
They're a little far, but...

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:54.320
I think I can catch something.

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:58.080
I'll be diving around here. Be careful, okay?

00:09:58.080 --> 00:09:59.260
I will!

00:09:59.960 --> 00:10:01.530
<i>I'm going to catch something!</i>

00:10:01.810 --> 00:10:04.110
<i>I'm going to be useful, too!</i>

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:07.690
You just watch me!

00:10:07.690 --> 00:10:09.030
Okay. Come on!

00:10:09.030 --> 00:10:10.750
I'll get you even if you're a tuna!

00:10:21.360 --> 00:10:22.970
I finally caught something.

00:10:23.550 --> 00:10:25.790
A black porgy is a more than
good enough catch.

00:10:26.190 --> 00:10:28.620
I wonder if Shion's caught something, too.

00:10:30.710 --> 00:10:33.580
She'll only be able to catch
things close to the surface,

00:10:33.580 --> 00:10:35.110
so at best she'd get a striped
mullet or something.

00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:37.000
Maybe I'll check on her...

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:41.720
A strong current flowing
from shore to offshore...

00:10:42.140 --> 00:10:43.700
A rip current...

00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:02.840
Shion!

00:11:02.840 --> 00:11:04.720
Hey!

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:09.380
Shion! Shion!

00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:15.130
There was something!

00:12:15.790 --> 00:12:17.630
Focus! Focus!

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:29.370
Next time, Case 11:
 "We Will Rescue Her."

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:31.100
<b>We Will Rescue Her</b>
